<gpx version="1.1" creator="test-fixture" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <trk>
    <name>dp-exact-group-all-same-positions</name>
    <trkseg>
      <!-- THREE points share the same timeMs AND same lat+lon+ele.
           They are NOT adjacent-exact-drops (no sequential pairs; all three have same time
           so isExactDuplicate between consecutive pairs is true for adj pair but we check
           if all-three form a same-time group allExact=true).
           Actually adj pair (0,1) IS an adjacent-exact-drop. Then (1,2) would be too.
           Point 1 goes to adjDropDropSet. Then group of 3 sharing time: points 0,1,2.
           But 1 is in adjDropDropSet → excluded from byTime. So group = [0, 2] only.
           isExactDuplicate(0, 2) → same time+lat+lon+ele → allExact=true → isExactGroup=true.
           Expected: two adjacent-exact-drop proposals (0→1, then after drop 1: NOT re-proposed since
           1 is excluded) + one insert proposal isExactGroup=true for [0,2].
           Actually, let me use NON-adjacent identical points that form an exact group:
           Stream: T+0, T+60(pt1), T+60(pt2), T+120 where pt1 and pt2 are non-adjacent in time
           but both at T+60.
           Hmm — let me just make 3 identical points all truly identical:
           Points 0,1,2 all at T=10:01, same lat/lon/ele.
           Adj pairs: (0,1) → adj-exact-drop, (1,2) → adj-exact-drop.
           adjDropDropSet = {1, 2}.
           byTime at T=10:01: filter out drops {1,2} → only [0] remains → size=1 → no insert.
           So for an exact-group insert, we need non-adjacent-in-stream same-time points.
           Better: points at same T but NOT gpxIndex+1 (stream-adjacent). E.g. gpxIndex 1 and 3 share T.
           Stream: T+0, T+60(pos1), T+30, T+60(pos2), T+120.
           The inner adj pairs: (0→1): different times. (1→2): T+60 > T+30 but T+30 ≠ T+60, not dup.
           (2→3): T+30 → T+60, different times. No adj-exact-drops.
           byTime at T+60: [1, 3]. isExactDuplicate(pt1, pt3)? pt1 and pt3 have same time,
           need same lat+lon+ele for allExact=true.
           Expected: insert isExactGroup=true, candidateGpxIndexes=[1,3].
           This tests the exact-group=true flag path. -->
      <trkpt lat="47.0000" lon="8.0000"><ele>500</ele><time>2024-01-01T10:00:00Z</time></trkpt>
      <trkpt lat="47.0010" lon="8.0010"><ele>501</ele><time>2024-01-01T10:01:00Z</time></trkpt>
      <trkpt lat="47.0005" lon="8.0005"><ele>500</ele><time>2024-01-01T10:00:30Z</time></trkpt>
      <trkpt lat="47.0010" lon="8.0010"><ele>501</ele><time>2024-01-01T10:01:00Z</time></trkpt>
      <trkpt lat="47.0020" lon="8.0020"><ele>502</ele><time>2024-01-01T10:02:00Z</time></trkpt>
    </trkseg>
  </trk>
